This report presents the initial observation of the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_L$ decay mode and provides evidence for the process $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_L$. The analysis is based on $3.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of data collected by the LHCb experiment at $\pp$ center-of-mass energies of 7 and 8 TeV. The measured branching fractions are given as
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{0} K^{\text{L} }_1)&=(4.19\pm0.43\pm0.15)\times10^{-4},
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^{\text{L} })&=(6.9\pm1.4\pm0.6)\times10^{-4},
\end{align*}
with the second uncertainties representing systematic errors.
